"""Measured optional SR interoperability update; retain historical test scopes."""
def apply(sections,sources,source,section,table,cite):
 source('S68','Streamline descriptor-heap incompatibility issue109','https://github.com/NVIDIA-RTX/Streamline/issues/109','Open issue describes black DLSS inputs with VK_EXT_descriptor_heap. Reporter confirms a conventional dummy descriptor-set bind before SR evaluation restores SR; FG cannot use the same explicit-evaluate workaround. Basix reproduced the black result and measured the SR workaround on its named local configuration.',kind='vendor issue / reporter workaround',rights='Linked discussion only; original Basix compatibility code is MIT. No SDK code copied.')
 sources[-1]['quality']='Acknowledged open issue and reporter workaround, independently reproduced only within Basix static SR fixture; not a universal fix.'
 source('S69','Basix actual DLSS SR validation receipt','https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/docs/dlss-results.json','Eight-case pinned-runtime harness:3actual SR frames,427x240→640x360,922320 input RGB checks and2073600 output RGB/native-engine comparisons. RMSE0.000347785,maxerror0.00146484. Whole-process Vulkan logs clean;3reviewed SDK manual-hook warnings per initialized process. No temporal-quality,RR,FG,resize or performance claim.',kind='local measured correctness',rights='Original Basix code/receipt MIT. Optional signed NVIDIA runtime has separate terms and is not vendored.')
 sources[-1]['quality']='Independent input oracle, native-copy versus engine comparison, per-frame poison/sentinel, no-op negative control and full-process logs.'
 by={s['id']:s for s in sections}
 by['summary']['body']+='<p><strong>SDK milestone completed:</strong> actual optional DLSS SR now evaluates on the NoGraphicsAPI-owned Vulkan device, followed by correct engine readback. This static interop gate uses an explicit descriptor-state workaround; temporal quality, RR and FG remain open. <a href="#dlss">See results and limits</a>.</p>'+cite('S68','S69')
 body=by['dlss']['body'];body=body.replace('No SDK has yet run in Basix.','The initial static SR evaluation has now passed; the broader renderer integration remains partial.').replace('<strong>Next actual SDK gate:</strong>','<strong>Implemented SDK boundary:</strong>')
 body+='''<h3>Actual SR interoperability · passed on the named local GPU</h3>
<p>The optional Windows target loads a signed, hash-pinned Streamline2.14.16 runtime from a separate local directory. Basix supplies a stable custom-engine ProjectID, pre-device extension/feature requirements, explicit color/depth/motion/exposure/output metadata, frame tokens and complete camera constants. No NVIDIA runtime is included in the repository.</p>
<p>Three real SR frames upscale427×240 to640×360. Before evaluation,922,320 RGB components match an independent constant-radiance input oracle. After evaluation,2,073,600 RGB components match an independent native FP16 image copy exactly; their expected-radiance RMSE is0.000347785 and maximum error0.00146484. Output images and both readback buffers are reset to sentinels/NaNs each frame. The no-evaluation control fails the oracle.</p>'''+cite('S69')+'''
<div class="callout"><strong>Required compatibility boundary</strong><p>Without a conventional descriptor-set handoff, the tested SDK returns success but writes black SR output with descriptor heaps active. Basix reproduces issue109 and binds an empty conventional set immediately before SR evaluation. It then rebinds both NoGraphicsAPI resource/sampler heaps, the pipeline and pointer-root data. This is a measured SR workaround, not a claim that FG works or the upstream issue is fixed.</p></div>'''+cite('S68','S69')+'''
<p>The full-process validation harness also caught initialization requirements outside the SDK’s returned SR list: core1.3 <code>privateData</code> and core1.4 <code>pushDescriptor</code>. Basix queries support before enabling them. It normalizes obsolete <code>VK_EXT_buffer_device_address</code> to the requested core1.2/KHR path, rather than enabling a forbidden EXT/core combination.</p>
<p>Eight cases cover actual evaluation, omitted-evaluation rejection, post-evaluation cleanup, unsupported extensions, relative runtime rejection, invalid signatures, Release validation refusal and the no-handoff control. Feature release and SDK shutdown must succeed before a passing receipt. Vulkan warning/error logs are clean; three SDK warnings concern unavailable automatic state-tracking hooks and are explicitly reviewed because Basix restores its own state.</p>
<p><strong>Limits:</strong> one Windows/RTX4090/NVIDIA617.42 configuration; constant radiance, zero motion and jitter, fixed resolution, no detail or temporal-quality acceptance. SDK resize, camera cuts, dynamic motion, fallback toggles, RR, FG and actual device loss remain unverified. The SDK still invokes its NGX bootstrap updater despite disabled OTA options; this is not an offline-runtime claim. Optional runtime redistribution requires its own NVIDIA terms/notices.</p>
<p><a href="dlss-results.json">Actual SDK receipt</a> · <a href="https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION.md">Build/stage/validate instructions</a></p>'''
 by['dlss']['body']=body
 by['implementation-status']['body']=by['implementation-status']['body'].replace('while actual SDK evaluation, OS minimize/device-loss handling','while temporal SDK quality, OS minimize/device-loss handling')
 by['implementation-status']['body']+='<p><strong>Actual SDK gate:</strong> M1b-sdk is completed for static SR and state restoration. M3-dlss remains partial because shared renderer guides, temporal quality, resets/fallbacks and RR are still open. The roadmap logbook retains the dated transitions and their receipts.</p>'+cite('S69')
 by['lessons']['body']+='<p><strong>Interop lesson:</strong> an SDK success code is not an image oracle. The descriptor-heap SR path returned success with black pixels; independent input/native/output checks exposed it. Full-process validation also found startup features outside the installed messenger’s scope. Preserve those failed controls alongside the working adapter.</p>'+cite('S68','S69')

def enrich_library(library):
 library['summary'].append('Actual static DLSS SR interoperability passes8cases with a measured descriptor-state workaround; temporal renderer quality remains unverified.')
 for f in library['findings']:
  if f['id']=='F15':f['claim']=f['claim'].replace('Actual SDK/device-loss remain open.','That earlier receipt does not test actual SDK/device loss; see F16 for the later SR gate.')
 library['findings'].append(dict(id='F16',title='Actual SR succeeds only with validated native-state handoff',question_ids=['Q2'],topic='rendering',claim='The actual optional SR gate passes a constant-radiance oracle and native/engine comparison after conventional descriptor-state handoff. Without it the tested SDK returns black output despite successful API calls.',evidence_type='measured',confidence='high',context='2026-10-28 Windows/RTX4090/NVIDIA617.42; signed pinned Streamline2.14.16 with process-local core/SyncVal.',strengths='Independent inputs/readbacks, per-frame poison, no-op/known-bug controls, explicit cleanup and full-process diagnostics.',limitations='Static fixed-resolution fixture only; reviewed manual-hook SDK warnings; no RR/FG/temporal/performance or shipping-license acceptance.',implications='Complete scoped M1b-sdk; retain M3-dlss and parentM1 as partial and proceed to renderer/motion/recovery gates.',tags=['DLSS','interop','validation','roadmap'],evidence=[dict(source_id=s,locator='Issue report/comments and receipt cases/gpu fields',relation='supports',note='Measured local SR only; upstream issue remains open.') for s in ['S68','S69']]))
 library['actions'][0].update(title='Build reference renderer and broaden recovery/temporal integration',finding_ids=['F16'],rationale='Static hardware rays and actual SR seams now pass; shared material/motion guides and real recovery remain open.',success_criterion='Reference material/PT outputs, camera/object motion, SDK resets/resize and separately scoped failure recovery pass independent tests.')
 library['scope_changes'].append('Completed actual static SR interoperability after reproducing issue109; retained original failed oracle and startup-validation evidence. Added visible status logbook and scoped transitions.')
 library['search_log'].append(dict(date='2026-10-28',phase='implementation update',engine='Pinned official SDK/source, NVIDIA issue109 and local Vulkan validation',query='Streamline descriptor_heap black SR input native interop',source_ids=['S68','S69'],outcome='Reproduced black output, independently validated legacy handoff and full engine-state restoration; broader DLSS quality remains pending.'))
